238"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - AutoDNA is an artificial intelligence (AI)-native autonomous biomolecular engineering laboratory targeting multi-objective experiments across diverse instruments, realizing the...", "display_url": "go.nature.com/47UJudb", "end": 123, "expanded_url": "https://go.nature.com/47UJudb", "images": [{"height": 1846, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120238325378228224/S1QISf-z?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1538}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120238325378228224/S1QISf-z?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 100, "status": 200, "title": "An AI-native experimental laboratory for autonomous biomolecular operations", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11228-6?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64326676&error=cookies_not_supported&code=5716982c-a8d6-4d13-9626-deeb944ea327", "url": "https://t.co/Pjwocl3gby"}]}, "id": "2120238311579042238", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4285, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "Nature research paper: An AI-native experimental laboratory for autonomous biomolecular operations\n\nhttps://t.co/Pjwocl3gby", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2120238311579042238"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:23:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120235801426464908"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Is self-enclosure life’s greatest trick? According to the lipid-first theory of the origin of life, a cell membrane gave primordial chemistry a place to gather.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/the-case-for-a…", "end": 151, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-case-for-a-bubble-at-lifes-start-20261110/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120172500231598080/JiyQOua9?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120172500231598080/JiyQOua9?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 128, "status": 200, "title": "The Case for a Bubble at Life’s Start | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-case-for-a-bubble-at-lifes-start-20261110/", "url": "https://t.co/U5h0rNkKBY"}]}, "id": "2120235801426464908", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2173, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Next up in Quanta’s Origins of Life Week: writer Perri Thaler explores whether early Earth was filled with life-giving bubbles. https://t.co/U5h0rNkKBY", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120235801426464908"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:22:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120235549604659501"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 93, "id": "2326120952", "start": 77, "username": "ScienceAdvances"}], "urls": [{"description": "Conversation is a core component of human social life. Many influential theories treat conversation as a linear system, i.e., the sum of its parts. However, linear accounts of semantic entrainment lose explanatory power at their upper limits: Discussing ...", "display_url": "scim.ag/4iBRaWI", "end": 265, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/4iBRaWI", "images": [{"height": 550, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118809413347602432/3PQD1Q1J?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 715}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118809413347602432/3PQD1Q1J?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 242, "status": 200, "title": "Pink noise in dyads’ semantic similarity trajectories predicts conversation enjoyment", "unwound_url": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.aeb2684?utm_campaign=ScienceMagazine&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=ownedSocial", "url": "https://t.co/m2vTAqxyRe"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/jdpfv2fGoo", "end": 289, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120235549604659501/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120235547343929344", "start": 266, "url": "https://t.co/jdpfv2fGoo"}]}, "id": "2120235549604659501", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 5768, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Good conversation between two people involves “pink noise,” according to new @ScienceAdvances research. This term refers to fluctuations in semantic similarities—alignments in speech patterns and word choice—across time scales during a chat. https://t.co/m2vTAqxyRe https://t.co/jdpfv2fGoo", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120235549604659501"}, {"author_id": "86626845", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:03:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120230975204708541"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 146, "id": "15862891", "start": 139, "username": "Nature"}], "urls": [{"description": "Nature - For years, researchers have studied people with a genetic predisposition to Alzheimer’s and other dementias. They might have even more to learn from those who don’t get the disease.", "display_url": "nature.com/articles/d4158…", "end": 171, "expanded_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03625-8", "images": [{"height": 675, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120117436305305600/ianV031N?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120117436305305600/ianV031N?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 148, "status": 200, "title": "Some people are resistant to dementia — here’s what their genes can teach us", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03625-8?error=cookies_not_supported&code=10d3855f-56c8-40bc-8633-2c151ea61dd3", "url": "https://t.co/9WqGD6yyG5"}]}, "id": "2120230975204708541", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 24, "impression_count": 8437, "like_count": 47, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "What accounts for genetic resistance to Alzheimer's disease and dementia?\nMany known protective gene variants are very instructive\nFeature @Nature \nhttps://t.co/9WqGD6yyG5", "url": "https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2120230975204708541"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:01:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120230402333798642"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A former Eli Lilly sales rep filed a lawsuit alleging she was fired after claiming the company was inappropriately promoting its Mounjaro diabetes drug to combat weight loss.", "display_url": "trib.al/1KW3j2N", "end": 198, "expanded_url": "https://trib.al/1KW3j2N", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120230409774448640/bHLMitD_?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120230409774448640/bHLMitD_?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 175, "status": 200, "title": "Former Eli Lilly rep claims she was fired for complaining about marketing of Mounjaro diabetes drug", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/pharmalot/2026/11/10/former-lilly-rep-claims-she-was-fired-for-complaining-about-marketing-of-mounjaro-diabetes-drug/?utm_campaign=twitter_organic&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social", "url": "https://t.co/G8STJ6XHlb"}]}, "id": "2120230402333798642", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1122, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A former Eli Lilly sales rep filed a lawsuit alleging she was fired after claiming the company was inappropriately promoting its Mounjaro diabetes drug to combat weight loss. https://t.co/G8STJ6XHlb", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120230402333798642"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:45:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120226247691083891"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Billionaire Bill Ackman as a bold plan to transform brain research, spurred by a tragic backstory.", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/11/09/bil…", "end": 81, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/09/bill-ackman-launches-new-brain-research-institute/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119874159702335488/IKq58NiX?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119874159702335488/IKq58NiX?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 58, "status": 200, "title": "Bill Ackman’s bold plan to transform brain research", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/09/bill-ackman-launches-new-brain-research-institute/", "url": "https://t.co/Euc75Ya1vF"}]}, "id": "2120226247691083891", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1110, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "If you’re blind, Bill Ackman wants to help you see again. https://t.co/Euc75Ya1vF", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120226247691083891"}, {"author_id": "15862891", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:41:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120225455240352226"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - Government-supported initiatives around the globe aim to change the PhD, with the goal of providing fresh talent to the private sector.", "display_url": "go.nature.com/3WzqNJA", "end": 159, "expanded_url": "https://go.nature.com/3WzqNJA", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120225460772626432/IEJgwshX?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120225460772626432/IEJgwshX?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 136, "status": 200, "title": "PhDs worldwide are having a shake up — why now?", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03017-y?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64369666&error=cookies_not_supported&code=e691172c-9abf-4427-a0bc-3bb7c16af0f8", "url": "https://t.co/lipm9cYlLu"}]}, "id": "2120225455240352226", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 5060, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Government-supported initiatives around the globe aim to change the PhD, with the goal of providing fresh talent to the private sector\n\nhttps://t.co/lipm9cYlLu", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2120225455240352226"}, {"author_id": "808633423300624384", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:38:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120224622977114523"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "This coming Wednesday, November 11, 2026, arXiv will be observing Veterans Day, a federal holiday in the United States. This will temporarily affect arXiv’s…", "display_url": "blog.arxiv.org/2026/11/06/ann…", "end": 152, "expanded_url": "https://blog.arxiv.org/2026/11/06/announcement-change-veterans-day/", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120224624650616832/owTYoySk?format=png&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120224624650616832/owTYoySk?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 129, "status": 200, "title": "Attention Authors: Temporary changes to announcement schedule due to upcoming US federal holiday", "unwound_url": "https://blog.arxiv.org/2026/11/06/announcement-change-veterans-day/", "url": "https://t.co/2uNfHW55n2"}]}, "id": "2120224622977114523", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 610, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Attention Authors: temporary disruption to the arXiv announcement schedule tomorrow for Veterans Day.\n\nMore details on the blog: https://t.co/2uNfHW55n2", "url": "https://x.com/arxiv/status/2120224622977114523"}, {"author_id": "15134240", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:22:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120220457190236607"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/GHhBtapeDR", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2120220457190236607/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120220451901145088", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/GHhBtapeDR"}]}, "id": "2120220457190236607", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 5689, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "As cancer rates rise among adults under the age of 55, researchers are looking for new methods of early cancer detection and prevention. An NIH-supported study found that faster biological aging of the whole body and specific organs can increase the risk of early-onset cancer. https://t.co/GHhBtapeDR", "url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2120220457190236607"}, {"author_id": "15862891", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:10:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120217589657854386"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - For years, researchers have studied people with a genetic predisposition to Alzheimer’s and other dementias. They might have even more to learn from those who don’t get the disease.", "display_url": "go.nature.com/4zDjrDn", "end": 175, "expanded_url": "https://go.nature.com/4zDjrDn", "images": [{"height": 675, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120217594770718720/pXfqwkwW?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120217594770718720/pXfqwkwW?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 152, "status": 200, "title": "Some people are resistant to dementia — here’s what their genes can teach us", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03625-8?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64369651&error=cookies_not_supported&code=b3ab7beb-4666-47e7-9f27-bfa79b04cfc7", "url": "https://t.co/A43niYptRZ"}]}, "id": "2120217589657854386", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 44, "impression_count": 9286, "like_count": 88, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 28}, "text": "The brain, it seems, has its own defence mechanisms against the toxic proteins that cause Alzheimer’s — mechanisms that scientists now hope to exploit\n\nhttps://t.co/A43niYptRZ", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2120217589657854386"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:06:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120216531216769439"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "In this edition of STAT Health Tech: Growing optimism around chatbots and men who avoid therapy, and highlights from the earnings season.", "display_url": "trib.al/2aJWZ4k", "end": 161, "expanded_url": "https://trib.al/2aJWZ4k", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120216537294397440/7YO0h7Qs?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120216537294397440/7YO0h7Qs?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 138, "status": 200, "title": "Men's use of chatbots for therapy, and earnings season highlights", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/10/chatbots-for-men-and-earnings-highlights-health-tech/?utm_campaign=twitter_organic&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social", "url": "https://t.co/2zfcbJuRaa"}]}, "id": "2120216531216769439", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1080, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "In this edition of STAT Health Tech: Growing optimism around chatbots and men who avoid therapy, and highlights from the earnings season. https://t.co/2zfcbJuRaa", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120216531216769439"}, {"author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:59:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120214667595268523"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A designed chemoenzymatic cascade reaction enables cell-free synthesis of starch from carbon dioxide.", "display_url": "scim.ag/4sPujLZ", "end": 269, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/4sPujLZ", "images": [{"height": 550, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120214672968220672/CyaItPJb?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 715}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120214672968220672/CyaItPJb?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 246, "status": 200, "title": "Cell-free chemoenzymatic starch synthesis from carbon dioxide", "unwound_url": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.abh4049?utm_campaign=ScienceMagazine&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=ownedSocial", "url": "https://t.co/GIaZfDwLSc"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/KSTpy4MmIN", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120214667595268523/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120214665263284224", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/KSTpy4MmIN"}]}, "id": "2120214667595268523", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 17, "impression_count": 7162, "like_count": 28, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "From carbon dioxide to starch—no plants required.\n\nIn Science, researchers developed a cell-free method of synthesizing starch from CO2 and hydrogen using a combination of chemical catalysts and a carefully selected set of enzymes. \n\nLearn more: https://t.co/GIaZfDwLSc https://t.co/KSTpy4MmIN", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2120214667595268523"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:58:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120214415152721999"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Bayer's drug is the first in a novel class of medications designed to prevent blood clots without increasing risk of bleeding.", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/11/09/car…", "end": 205, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/09/cardiovascular-stroke-recurrence-bayer-drug-fda-approval/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119923980270235648/3WtWZinI?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119923980270235648/3WtWZinI?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 182, "status": 200, "title": "FDA approves novel Bayer drug to reduce recurrence of stroke", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/09/cardiovascular-stroke-recurrence-bayer-drug-fda-approval/", "url": "https://t.co/0SVuxOEJ2K"}]}, "id": "2120214415152721999", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1175, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "The FDA approved Bayer’s drug to reduce recurrence of stroke, making available the first in a novel class of medications that hold the promise of preventing blood clots more safely. https://t.co/0SVuxOEJ2K", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120214415152721999"}, {"author_id": "28164923", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:57:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120214311918334341"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The seven insiders are each set to sell around $250 million worth of shares and keep total voting control.", "display_url": "on.wsj.com/4kPjmYy", "end": 159, "expanded_url": "https://on.wsj.com/4kPjmYy", "images": [{"height": 640, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120214313533153281/ldhFmKQ_?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120214313533153281/ldhFmKQ_?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 136, "status": 200, "title": "Anthropic Founders’ Stakes Are Worth $18 Billion Apiece at IPO Price", "unwound_url": "https://www.wsj.com/finance/anthropic-founders-stakes-are-worth-18-billion-apiece-at-ipo-price-2c746365?reflink=e2twmkts", "url": "https://t.co/skCJrj5jGI"}]}, "id": "2120214311918334341", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5194, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Anthropic’s seven founders plan to cash out about $250 million apiece in the IPO—leaving them with stakes worth around $18 billion each https://t.co/skCJrj5jGI", "url": "https://x.com/WSJmarkets/status/2120214311918334341"}, {"author_id": "15862891", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:39:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120209665086673341"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Nature - The cash infusion, earmarked for immunology studies, is the largest ever for science authorized by a US public vote — but it has drawn criticism.", "display_url": "go.nature.com/4BVRLem", "end": 169, "expanded_url": "https://go.nature.com/4BVRLem", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120209669935267840/5CJE2D5k?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1066}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120209669935267840/5CJE2D5k?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 146, "status": 200, "title": "California votes to give record $8.4 billion to medical research", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03635-6?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64369356&error=cookies_not_supported&code=e6250dde-9677-4df1-89a9-8b31867c9b2f", "url": "https://t.co/oMRZVyAnTo"}]}, "id": "2120209665086673341", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 5123, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "The cash infusion, earmarked for immunology studies, is the largest ever for science authorized by a US public vote — but it has drawn criticism\n\nhttps://t.co/oMRZVyAnTo", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2120209665086673341"}, {"author_id": "407985006", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:28:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120206865778745532"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Measurements on micrometer-scale cadmium samples provide definitive evidence of an unusual charge-transport regime in a 3D metal.", "display_url": "go.aps.org/3WDnOzJ", "end": 272, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/3WDnOzJ", "images": [{"height": 250, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120081883018989570/0JuV9mlx?format=png&name=orig", "width": 500}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120081883018989570/0JuV9mlx?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 249, "status": 200, "title": "The Gurzhi Effect Reaches Three Dimensions", "unwound_url": "https://physics.aps.org/articles/v19/148", "url": "https://t.co/l404BV04Hd"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/r1O5j985mp", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/PhysicsMagazine/status/2120206865778745532/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120206863576764416", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/r1O5j985mp"}]}, "id": "2120206865778745532", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 414, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "In 1963, Radii Gurzhi predicted that some metals might behave more like classical liquids, with conductivity increasing as the temperature rises. A study now provides definitive evidence of this effect in a 3D elemental metal. \n\nRead the Viewpoint: https://t.co/l404BV04Hd https://t.co/r1O5j985mp", "url": "https://x.com/PhysicsMagazine/status/2120206865778745532"}, {"article": {"title": "NIH helped pave the way for two new therapeutics for people with ultra-rare bone disease"}, "author_id": "15134240", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:16:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120203991963590930"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2120…", "end": 235, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2120201753828454400", "start": 212, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2120201753828454400", "url": "https://t.co/vz8ePArcaH"}]}, "id": "2120203991963590930", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6416, "like_count": 21, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "NIH-supported research spanning decades helped pave the way for new treatment options for people living with fibrodysplasia ossificans progressiva (FOP), an ulta-rare and devastating genetic disease.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/vz8ePArcaH", "url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2120203991963590930"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:10:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120202485209985044"], "entitie